Hello and Thank You!&nbsp;<br />
Thank you for stepping up to host a blood drive this summer! &nbsp;The summer months are a critical time for our nation&#39;s blood supply, so your efforts to bring family, friends and community together to donate blood is greatly appreciated.<br />
<br />
Your role as Blood Drive Coordinator will be to recruit donors to come to your drive and to find a suitable place for the blood drive.&nbsp;<br />
Step 1: &nbsp;Interest Survey<br />
I am attaching an Interest Survey that you can begin to prospect your personal contacts to determine who will donate blood Step 2: &nbsp;Location<br />
&nbsp;A large space like a gymnasium or suitable space of 1000 square feet or more, with temperature control (must be around 68 - 73 degrees inside), must have bathrooms, and preferably no stairs (elevators are great! ). &nbsp;<br />
If we use a Blood mobile Bus, then the site must be flat and have ample parking for donors. Also, must have indoor access to restrooms.&nbsp;<br />
<br />
Will you be available this evening to chat? &nbsp;Or anytime between now and Saturday afternoon.&nbsp;<br />
<br />
Thanks,<br />
<br />
